NAME
    lang-set - query or change the selected global language

SYNOPSIS
    lang-set
    lang-set <locale>

DESCRIPTION
    With no operands, lang-set writes the locale selected by the sys language
    selector and a newline.

    With one locale operand, lang-set validates every materialized global
    res/<owner>/lang tree before changing any selector. The requested locale
    must exist in every participating tree and every existing current selector
    must be a valid local relative symbolic link.

    Non-sys selectors are updated first and the sys selector is updated last.
    On an ordinary update error the command attempts rollback. Successful
    selection writes no output.

    Package-local language resources are not modified.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m lang-set [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   Query or selection succeeded.
    Non-zero status indicates invalid invocation, invalid selector/locale or an
        operational update failure.

SEE ALSO
    lang
